# Rank 1215 / CVE-2022-2111 (GHSA-fr2w-mp56-g4xp): InvenTree lets an
# authenticated user attach an arbitrary file to a part/build/order/stock
# record with no restriction on its type. The bootstrap-table formatter for
# every attachment column (InvenTree/templates/js/translated/attachment.js's
# loadAttachmentTable, InvenTree/templates/js/translated/stock.js's
# loadStockTestResultsTable) turned that file's URL into a plain anchor via
# InvenTree/templates/js/translated/tables.js's renderLink(text, url,
# options): `return '<a href="' + url + '">' + text + '</a>';`. A same-origin
# `<a href>` with no `download` attribute lets the browser navigate to and
# render the response inline, so an attachment saved as an .html file with
# embedded <script> ran with the application's own origin the moment another
# user clicked its link (CWE-434).
#
# The fixed revision (in inventree/inventree) never restricts the
# uploadable extension; it makes renderLink take a `download: true` option
# that appends a `download='<filename>'` attribute, and switches both
# attachment-link call sites to pass it — attachment.js's loadAttachmentTable
# and stock.js's loadStockTestResultsTable, whose own inline
# `<a href='${row.attachment}'>` template literal becomes a renderLink call
# too — so the browser always saves the file instead of opening it in the
# current tab. No Python file changed for this specific advisory (the same
# squash commit's admin.py/version.py changes are for two other bundled
# GHSAs, CSV formula injection and bootstrap-table HTML escaping); the entire
# fix for CVE-2022-2111 itself is these three JavaScript shapes.
#
# repo! resolved: GHSA-fr2w-mp56-g4xp's own "For more information" section
# links http://github.com/inventree/inventree, and the fixing commit
# 26bf51c20a1c9b3130ac5dd2e17649bece5ff84f exists in inventree/inventree
# (`gh api /repos/inventree/inventree/commits/26bf51c...` resolves; the same
# SHA against inventree/inventree-python 404s). OSV's affected-package entry
# lists PyPI `inventree`, which is the pip name inventree-python's own
# setup.py publishes under — a coincidental name collision between the
# server's PyPI-irrelevant CVE metadata and the client library's package
# name, not a second repository carrying the same fix. inventree-python is a
# thin REST client (session/part/stock wrapper classes over `requests`); it
# has no bootstrap-table rendering, no renderLink, and no attachment-link
# templates for this vulnerability to live in. pool.tsv rank 1215 is
# unchanged.
#
# ATTENTION, vocabulary gap. `vyql match` on both revisions of a repro
# faithful to tables.js's renderLink, attachment.js's loadAttachmentTable and
# stock.js's loadStockTestResultsTable labels nothing at the anchor call
# sites (no source, sink, or control), and a bounded scan of the real
# checkout's InvenTree/templates/js/translated/ directory (timeout 180,
# --max-ram 6GB, --cache off, three runs per revision; javascript:21
# textpattern:21) reports 248 findings at the vulnerable revision and 196 at
# the fixed one, none of them at attachment.js, at renderLink itself, or at
# stock.js's attachment formatter — VYQL-INJ-004 (code.DomInput ->
# code.HtmlRender) fires nearby, on modals.js, part.js, notification.js and
# order.js, so the general DOM-XSS rule is reachable in this exact file set,
# but never on renderLink's own call sites, because `value`/`row.attachment`
# there is data read back from an inventreeGet() API response rather than a
# bound code.DomInput source, and `renderLink`'s `<a href>` build is not a
# recognized code.HtmlRender-relevant string shape either. Normalised over
# line numbers the two revisions' finding sets are identical (44 distinct
# rule/source/sink shapes, zero difference in either direction); the raw
# 52-finding drop is duplicate multiplicity collapsing under the same
# commit's bundled bootstrap-table HTML-escaping hunk, not discrimination for
# this advisory. No existing concept models this weakness's actual mechanism:
# every CWE-434 concept in this ontology (code.FileUpload, code.UnsafeUpload,
# code.IncompleteFileExtensionValidation and its per-CMS variants) judges
# whether an uploaded file's *extension* is restricted before it is saved to
# disk, which is not what InvenTree's own fix does — it accepts any
# extension and instead forces the browser to download rather than render
# the file. The two closest later additions do not reach it either:
# code.UploadDeclaredResponseContentType is the server-side twin (a stored
# file's recorded content type served inline), whose only JavaScript binding
# keys on the Web `new Response(...)` constructor this jQuery-era application
# never uses — its attachments are Django MEDIA served outside application
# code — and which would fire on both revisions anyway since this fix is
# entirely client-side; and code.StoredUrlHrefAttributeXss has a single PHP
# binding keyed on GLPI's own Toolbox.formatOutputWebLink helper and
# `fields['website']`-style stored-URL fields, and models a URL that is
# itself the payload, whereas InvenTree's anchor URL is a benign same-origin
# path and the payload is the served file's content. That leaves a
# client-side HTML-attribute question (does this anchor to a same-origin,
# arbitrarily-typed resource carry `download`), with no concept for the
# attribute in any language and no library-documented helper to bind.
# A new concept was not minted: `renderLink` is an
# application-private helper with no public documentation to write a binding
# from — the genericity test in AGENTS.md ("would someone who has never seen
# this CVE write the same binding from the library's documentation alone?")
# fails outright, since there is no library here, only InvenTree's own JS.
# The generalizable version of the rule — "an anchor to a same-origin,
# type-unrestricted user-uploaded file must carry `download` or the response
# must set Content-Disposition: attachment" — would need a new taint source
# for "URL naming an uploaded file" that has no natural home in the current
# ontology and no way to discriminate from any other same-origin link without
# risking false positives on ordinary internal navigation, so it is design
# work, not a bounded binding or rule change, and was not attempted.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-vocabulary-gap, both revisions reject
# VYQL-INJ-004, the nearest rule reachable in this exact file set.

test "rank1215: renderLink builds a plain <a href> with no download attribute, so an HTML attachment renders inline"
  lang javascript
  reject VYQL-INJ-004
  file tables.js
  ```
  function renderLink(text, url, options={}) {
      if (url === null || url === undefined || url === '') {
          return text;
      }

      var max_length = options.max_length || -1;

      if ((max_length > 0) && (text.length > max_length)) {
          var slice_length = (max_length - 3) / 2;
          var text_start = text.slice(0, slice_length);
          var text_end = text.slice(-slice_length);
          text = `${text_start}...${text_end}`;
      }

      return '<a href="' + url + '">' + text + '</a>';
  }
  ```
  file attachment.js
  ```
  function loadAttachmentTable(url, options) {

      options.table.inventreeTable({
          url: url,
          columns: [
              {
                  field: 'attachment',
                  title: 'File',
                  formatter: function(value, row) {
                      if (value) {
                          var split = value.split('/');
                          var filename = split[split.length - 1];
                          var icon = attachmentIcon(filename);
                          var html = `<span class='fas ${icon}'></span> ${filename}`;

                          return renderLink(html, value);
                      } else if (row.link) {
                          var html = `<span class='fas fa-link'></span> ${row.link}`;
                          return renderLink(html, row.link);
                      } else {
                          return '-';
                      }
                  }
              }
          ]
      });
  }
  ```
  file stock.js
  ```
  function loadStockTestResultsTable(table, options) {

      table.inventreeTable({
          url: options.url,
          columns: [
              {
                  field: 'value',
                  title: 'Value',
                  formatter: function(value, row) {
                      var html = value;

                      if (row.attachment) {
                          html += `<a href='${row.attachment}'><span class='fas fa-file-alt float-right'></span></a>`;
                      }

                      return html;
                  }
              }
          ]
      });
  }
  ```

test "rank1215: renderLink({download: true}) forces the browser to save the attachment instead of rendering it"
  lang javascript
  reject VYQL-INJ-004
  file tables.js
  ```
  function renderLink(text, url, options={}) {
      if (url === null || url === undefined || url === '') {
          return text;
      }

      var max_length = options.max_length || -1;

      var extra = '';

      if (options.download) {
          var fn = url.split('/').at(-1);
          extra += ` download='${fn}'`;
      }

      if ((max_length > 0) && (text.length > max_length)) {
          var slice_length = (max_length - 3) / 2;
          var text_start = text.slice(0, slice_length);
          var text_end = text.slice(-slice_length);
          text = `${text_start}...${text_end}`;
      }

      return `<a href='${url}'${extra}>${text}</a>`;
  }
  ```
  file attachment.js
  ```
  function loadAttachmentTable(url, options) {

      options.table.inventreeTable({
          url: url,
          columns: [
              {
                  field: 'attachment',
                  title: 'File',
                  formatter: function(value, row) {
                      if (value) {
                          var split = value.split('/');
                          var filename = split[split.length - 1];
                          var icon = attachmentIcon(filename);
                          var html = `<span class='fas ${icon}'></span> ${filename}`;

                          return renderLink(html, value, {download: true});
                      } else if (row.link) {
                          var html = `<span class='fas fa-link'></span> ${row.link}`;
                          return renderLink(html, row.link);
                      } else {
                          return '-';
                      }
                  }
              }
          ]
      });
  }
  ```
  file stock.js
  ```
  function loadStockTestResultsTable(table, options) {

      table.inventreeTable({
          url: options.url,
          columns: [
              {
                  field: 'value',
                  title: 'Value',
                  formatter: function(value, row) {
                      var html = value;

                      if (row.attachment) {
                          var text = `<span class='fas fa-file-alt float-right'></span>`;
                          html += renderLink(text, row.attachment, {download: true});
                      }

                      return html;
                  }
              }
          ]
      });
  }
  ```
